IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 17 and 18 -- forming a company, the kinds of company, the bar on large unregistered associations,
-- the end of the guarantee company with a share capital, and the private company. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- This module supplies the keel's seams for s 17(6) (the 2-year period has expired) and s 18 (the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18).
-- The Registrar appears only as the holder of the duty in s 17(9); there is no seat for the Registrar.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".

§ `Section 17: formation of companies`

-- src:3533 | 17.—(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, any person may,
-- src:3534 | whether alone or together with another person, by subscribing the
-- src:3535 | person’s name or their names to a constitution and complying with
-- src:3536 | the requirements as to registration, form an incorporated company.
@ref s 17(1) (src:3533-3536)
GIVEN `the person has subscribed the person's name, or their names together with another person's, to a constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has complied with the requirements as to registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) the person may form an incorporated company` MEANS
    IF `the person has subscribed the person's name, or their names together with another person's, to a constitution` AND `the person has complied with the requirements as to registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): any person may form an incorporated company "by subscribing the person's name or their names to a constitution and complying with the requirements as to registration"; the text says nothing of forming one another way, and the power is "Subject to the provisions of this Act"

-- (2): "A company may be (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ...": the list is not closed with "only".
-- src:3540 | (2) A company may be —
-- src:3542 | (a) a company limited by shares;
-- src:3544 | (b) a company limited by guarantee; or
-- src:3546 | (c) an unlimited company.
@ref s 17(2) (src:3540-3546)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) a company may be of this kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER liability
    WHEN `limited by shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `limited by guarantee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `unlimited` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A company may be (a) a company limited by shares; (b) a company limited by guarantee; or (c) an unlimited company" does not say "only"; a company limited both by shares and by guarantee is left to section 4(1) and to subsection (5)

-- (3) and (4): one function, because the text names no bearer and (4) reads down (3). JUST TRUE means the formation is barred.
-- The bar is about "more than 20 persons" and "any business that has for its object the acquisition of gain": a body outside that scope is NOTHING (the text does not speak of it).
-- src:3551 | (3) No company, association or partnership consisting of more than
-- src:3552 | 20 persons may be formed for the purpose of carrying on any business
-- src:3553 | that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the company,
-- src:3554 | association or partnership, or by the individual members thereof,
-- src:3555 | unless it is registered as a company under this Act, or is formed
-- src:3556 | pursuant to some other written law in Singapore or letters patent.
-- src:3558 | (4) So much of subsection (3) as prohibits the formation of an
-- src:3559 | association or a partnership consisting of more than 20 persons does
-- src:3560 | not apply to an association or a partnership formed solely or mainly
-- src:3561 | for the purpose of carrying on any profession or calling which under
-- src:3562 | the provisions of any written law may be exercised only by persons
-- src:3563 | who possess the qualifications laid down in such written law for the
-- src:3564 | purpose of carrying on that profession or calling.
@ref s 17(3) and (4) (src:3551-3564)
GIVEN `the number of persons the body consists of` IS A NUMBER
      `the body is formed for the purpose of carrying on a business that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the body or by its individual members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is registered as a company under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is formed pursuant to some other written law in Singapore or letters patent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is an association or a partnership formed solely or mainly for the purpose of carrying on a profession or calling which under a written law may be exercised only by persons who possess the qualifications laid down in that law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(3) and (4) the formation of the body is barred` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons the body consists of` GREATER THAN 20 AND `the body is formed for the purpose of carrying on a business that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the body or by its individual members`
    THEN (IF `the body is registered as a company under this Act` OR `the body is formed pursuant to some other written law in Singapore or letters patent`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is registered as a company under this Act, or is formed pursuant to some other written law in Singapore or letters patent" (an "unless", met)
          ELSE (IF (NOT `the body is a company`) AND `the body is an association or a partnership formed solely or mainly for the purpose of carrying on a profession or calling which under a written law may be exercised only by persons who possess the qualifications laid down in that law`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "So much of subsection (3) as prohibits the formation of an association or a partnership consisting of more than 20 persons does not apply to an association or a partnership formed solely or mainly for the purpose of carrying on any profession or calling" (a flat negative)
                ELSE JUST TRUE))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a body "consisting of more than 20 persons" formed to carry on "any business that has for its object the acquisition of gain"; the text says nothing of a body of 20 or fewer persons or of one with no such object

-- src:3566 | (5) As from 15 August 1984, no company limited by guarantee with
-- src:3567 | a share capital may be registered under this Act.
@ref s 17(5) (src:3566-3567)
GIVEN `the company is a company limited by guarantee with a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of registration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(5) the company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act` MEANS
    IF `the company is a company limited by guarantee with a share capital` AND `the date of registration` AT LEAST (Date 15 8 1984)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As from 15 August 1984, no company limited by guarantee with a share capital may be registered under this Act" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks of "a company limited by guarantee with a share capital" registered "As from 15 August 1984"; the text says nothing of any other company or of an earlier registration

-- src:3569 | (6) The prohibition referred to in subsection (5) does not affect a
-- src:3570 | company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is
-- src:3571 | registered as such before 15 August 1984 and section 38(2) continues
-- src:3572 | to apply to a company so registered; but any such company must,
-- src:3573 | within 2 years of that date, elect to convert and re‑register that
-- src:3574 | company either as a company limited by shares or as a company
-- src:3575 | limited by guarantee.
@ref s 17(6) (src:3569-3575)
GIVEN `the company is a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and was registered as such before 15 August 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(6) the prohibition in subsection (5) affects the company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and was registered as such before 15 August 1984`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The prohibition referred to in subsection (5) does not affect a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is registered as such before 15 August 1984" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks only of "a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is registered as such before 15 August 1984"; the text says nothing of any other company

-- src:3569 | (6) The prohibition referred to in subsection (5) does not affect a
-- src:3570 | company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is
-- src:3571 | registered as such before 15 August 1984 and section 38(2) continues
-- src:3572 | to apply to a company so registered; but any such company must,
-- src:3573 | within 2 years of that date, elect to convert and re‑register that
-- src:3574 | company either as a company limited by shares or as a company
-- src:3575 | limited by guarantee.
@ref s 17(6) (src:3569-3575)
GIVEN `the company is a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and was registered as such before 15 August 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(6) section 38(2) continues to apply to the company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and was registered as such before 15 August 1984`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 38(2) continues to apply to a company so registered"; the text says nothing of any other company

-- "within 2 years of that date" (15 August 1984): 730 days, 1985 and 1986 having no 29 February (convention P1; fork line F-H-P2 reads the day itself as in time).
-- src:3569 | (6) The prohibition referred to in subsection (5) does not affect a
-- src:3570 | company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is
-- src:3571 | registered as such before 15 August 1984 and section 38(2) continues
-- src:3572 | to apply to a company so registered; but any such company must,
-- src:3573 | within 2 years of that date, elect to convert and re‑register that
-- src:3574 | company either as a company limited by shares or as a company
-- src:3575 | limited by guarantee.
@ref s 17(6) (src:3569-3575)
GIVEN `the company is a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and was registered as such before 15 August 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company elects to convert and re-register` IS A DATE
      `the election is to be a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(6) the company has elected within 2 years of 15 August 1984 to convert and re-register as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the company is a company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and was registered as such before 15 August 1984`
    THEN (IF `the date the company elects to convert and re-register` AT LEAST (Date 15 8 1984) AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 15 8 1984) `the date the company elects to convert and re-register` 2 Years AND `the election is to be a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any such company must, within 2 years of that date, elect to convert and re-register that company either as a company limited by shares or as a company limited by guarantee" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the last day is 15 August 1986)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is on "any such company"; the text says nothing of any other company

-- The seam the keel asks for (PLAN.md section 4, table A): "the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired".
-- src:3569 | (6) The prohibition referred to in subsection (5) does not affect a
-- src:3570 | company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is
-- src:3571 | registered as such before 15 August 1984 and section 38(2) continues
-- src:3572 | to apply to a company so registered; but any such company must,
-- src:3573 | within 2 years of that date, elect to convert and re‑register that
-- src:3574 | company either as a company limited by shares or as a company
-- src:3575 | limited by guarantee.
@ref s 17(6) (src:3569-3575)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(6) the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` MEANS
    `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` (Date 15 8 1984) 2 Years

-- src:3577 | (7) The conversion of a company referred to in subsection (6) is
-- src:3578 | effected by lodging with the Registrar a special resolution
-- src:3579 | determining the conversion of the company from a company
-- src:3580 | limited by guarantee with a share capital to a company limited by
-- src:3581 | shares or to a company limited by guarantee (as the case may be) and
-- src:3582 | altering its constitution to the extent that is necessary to bring them
-- src:3583 | into conformity with the requirements of this Act relating to the
-- src:3584 | constitution of a company limited by shares or of a company limited
-- src:3585 | by guarantee, as the case may be.
@ref s 17(7) (src:3577-3585)
GIVEN `the company is a company referred to in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a special resolution determining the conversion of the company has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution has been altered to the extent necessary to bring it into conformity with the requirements of this Act for the kind of company to which it converts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(7) the conversion of the company is effected` MEANS
    IF `the company is a company referred to in subsection (6)` AND `a special resolution determining the conversion of the company has been lodged with the Registrar` AND `the constitution has been altered to the extent necessary to bring it into conformity with the requirements of this Act for the kind of company to which it converts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the conversion "is effected by lodging with the Registrar a special resolution ... and altering its constitution"; the text does not say "only", and it says nothing of any other company

-- (8): "On compliance ... and on the issue by the Registrar of a notice of incorporation ... the company becomes a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee, as the case may be."
-- src:3589 | (8) On compliance by a company with subsection (7) and on the
-- src:3590 | issue by the Registrar of a notice of incorporation of the company in
-- src:3591 | accordance with the special resolution, the company becomes a
-- src:3596 | company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee, as the
-- src:3597 | case may be.
@ref s 17(8) (src:3589-3597)
GIVEN `the company has complied with subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has issued a notice of incorporation of the company in accordance with the special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of company the special resolution determines` IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Liability of members`
`s 17(8) the kind of company the company becomes` MEANS
    IF `the company has complied with subsection (7)` AND `the Registrar has issued a notice of incorporation of the company in accordance with the special resolution`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the kind of company the special resolution determines`
          WHEN `limited by shares` THEN JUST `limited by shares`
          WHEN `limited by guarantee` THEN JUST `limited by guarantee`
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company becomes a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee, as the case may be"; the text names no other result
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company becomes so "On compliance ... and on the issue by the Registrar of a notice of incorporation"; the text says nothing of a company that has not yet complied (a failed "On" gate returns no value)

-- src:3599 | (9) Upon the application of a company and payment of the
-- src:3600 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a
-- src:3601 | certificate of confirmation of incorporation.
@ref s 17(9) (src:3599-3601)
GIVEN `the company has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation" (a duty whose "upon" gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 18: private company`

-- (1)(b): "(counting joint holders of shares as one person and not counting any person in the employment of the company or of its subsidiary or any person who while previously in the employment ... was and thereafter has continued to be a member of the company)".
-- src:3612 | (b) limits to not more than 50 the number of its members
-- src:3613 | (counting joint holders of shares as one person and not
-- src:3614 | counting any person in the employment of the company or
-- src:3615 | of its subsidiary or any person who while previously in the
-- src:3616 | employment of the company or of its subsidiary was and
-- src:3617 | thereafter has continued to be a member of the company).
@ref s 18(1) (src:3612-3617)
GIVEN `the number of persons who hold shares, each joint holding counted once` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those persons who are in the employment of the company or of its subsidiary` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those persons who, while previously in the employment of the company or of its subsidiary, were and thereafter have continued to be members of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(1)(b) the number of members counted against the limit` MEANS
    `the number of persons who hold shares, each joint holding counted once` - `the number of those persons who are in the employment of the company or of its subsidiary` - `the number of those persons who, while previously in the employment of the company or of its subsidiary, were and thereafter have continued to be members of the company`

-- src:3607 | 18.—(1) A company having a share capital may be incorporated as
-- src:3608 | a private company if its constitution —
-- src:3610 | (a) restricts the right to transfer its shares; and
-- src:3612 | (b) limits to not more than 50 the number of its members
-- src:3613 | (counting joint holders of shares as one person and not
-- src:3614 | counting any person in the employment of the company or
-- src:3615 | of its subsidiary or any person who while previously in the
-- src:3616 | employment of the company or of its subsidiary was and
-- src:3617 | thereafter has continued to be a member of the company).
@ref s 18(1) (src:3607-3617)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution restricts the right to transfer its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members to which the constitution limits the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the company may be incorporated as a private company` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital`
    THEN (IF `the constitution restricts the right to transfer its shares` AND `the number of members to which the constitution limits the company` AT MOST 50
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company may be incorporated as a private company "if its constitution (a) restricts the right to transfer its shares; and (b) limits to not more than 50 the number of its members"; the text says nothing of a constitution that does not (grant ruling, limit 1)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence opens "A company having a share capital"; the text says nothing of a company with none

-- The seam the keel asks for (PLAN.md section 4, table A): "the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18".
-- True when the company has a share capital, its constitution restricts the transfer of its shares and limits its members to not more than 50, and the notice of incorporation states that it is a private company (section 19(4)).
-- src:3607 | 18.—(1) A company having a share capital may be incorporated as
-- src:3608 | a private company if its constitution —
-- src:3610 | (a) restricts the right to transfer its shares; and
-- src:3612 | (b) limits to not more than 50 the number of its members
-- src:3613 | (counting joint holders of shares as one person and not
-- src:3614 | counting any person in the employment of the company or
-- src:3615 | of its subsidiary or any person who while previously in the
-- src:3616 | employment of the company or of its subsidiary was and
-- src:3617 | thereafter has continued to be a member of the company).
@ref s 18(1) (src:3607-3617)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution restricts the right to transfer its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members to which the constitution limits the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice of incorporation states that the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the company was incorporated as a private company by virtue of section 18` MEANS
        `the company has a share capital`
    AND `the constitution restricts the right to transfer its shares`
    AND `the number of members to which the constitution limits the company` AT MOST 50
    AND `the notice of incorporation states that the company is a private company`

-- (2): "the constitution of the company is deemed to include each such restriction or limitation that is not so included".
DECLARE `s 18(2) restriction or limitation` IS ONE OF
    `s 18(2) a restriction on the right to transfer its shares`
    `s 18(2) a limitation on the number of its members`
    `s 18(2) any other provision`

-- src:3621 | (2) Where, on 29 December 1967, the constitution of a company
-- src:3622 | that is a private company by virtue of paragraph (a) of the definition
-- src:3623 | of “private company” in section 4(1) does not contain the restrictions
-- src:3624 | and limitations required by subsection (1) to be included in the
-- src:3625 | constitution of a company that may be incorporated as a private
-- src:3626 | company, the constitution of the company is deemed to include each
-- src:3627 | such restriction or limitation that is not so included and a restriction
-- src:3628 | on the right to transfer its shares that is so deemed to be included in its
-- src:3629 | constitution is deemed to be a restriction that prohibits the transfer of
-- src:3630 | shares except to a person approved by the directors of the company.
@ref s 18(2) (src:3621-3630)
GIVEN `on 29 December 1967 the company is a private company by virtue of paragraph (a) of the definition of "private company" in section 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution does not contain the restrictions and limitations required by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A `s 18(2) restriction or limitation`
      `the constitution already contains the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the constitution is deemed to include the provision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `on 29 December 1967 the company is a private company by virtue of paragraph (a) of the definition of "private company" in section 4(1)`) OR (NOT `the constitution does not contain the restrictions and limitations required by subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on 29 December 1967, the constitution of a company that is a private company by virtue of paragraph (a) of the definition of 'private company' in section 4(1) does not contain the restrictions and limitations required by subsection (1) ..., the constitution of the company is deemed to include each such restriction or limitation" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))
    ELSE (CONSIDER provision
          WHEN `s 18(2) a restriction on the right to transfer its shares` THEN (IF `the constitution already contains the provision` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "each such restriction or limitation that is not so included" is deemed included; the text says nothing of one already included
          WHEN `s 18(2) a limitation on the number of its members` THEN (IF `the constitution already contains the provision` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): as above
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of "each such restriction or limitation" as is "required by subsection (1)"; the text says nothing of any other provision

-- src:3626 | company, the constitution of the company is deemed to include each
-- src:3627 | such restriction or limitation that is not so included and a restriction
-- src:3628 | on the right to transfer its shares that is so deemed to be included in its
-- src:3629 | constitution is deemed to be a restriction that prohibits the transfer of
-- src:3630 | shares except to a person approved by the directors of the company.
@ref s 18(2) (src:3626-3630)
GIVEN `the restriction is a restriction on the right to transfer shares deemed to be included under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to a person approved by the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the deemed restriction prohibits the transfer of shares` MEANS
    IF `the restriction is a restriction on the right to transfer shares deemed to be included under subsection (2)`
    THEN (IF `the transfer is to a person approved by the directors of the company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to be a restriction that prohibits the transfer of shares except to a person approved by the directors of the company" (an "except", met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deemed content is stated for "a restriction on the right to transfer its shares that is so deemed to be included"; the text says nothing of any other restriction

-- src:3634 | (3) Where a restriction or limitation deemed to be included in the
-- src:3635 | constitution of a company under subsection (2) is inconsistent with
-- src:3636 | any provision already included in the constitution of the company,
-- src:3637 | that restriction or limitation, to the extent of the inconsistency,
-- src:3638 | prevails.
@ref s 18(3) (src:3634-3638)
GIVEN `the restriction or limitation is deemed to be included in the constitution under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is inconsistent with a provision already included in the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(3) the deemed restriction or limitation prevails over the provision to the extent of the inconsistency` MEANS
    IF `the restriction or limitation is deemed to be included in the constitution under subsection (2)` AND `it is inconsistent with a provision already included in the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a restriction or limitation deemed to be included in the constitution of a company under subsection (2) is inconsistent with any provision already included in the constitution of the company, that restriction or limitation, to the extent of the inconsistency, prevails" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

-- src:3642 | (4) A private company may, by special resolution, alter any
-- src:3643 | restriction on the right to transfer its shares included, or deemed to
-- src:3648 | be included, in its constitution or any limitation on the number of its
-- src:3649 | members included, or deemed to be included, in its constitution, but
-- src:3650 | not so that the constitution of the company ceases to include the
-- src:3651 | limitation required by subsection (1)(b) to be included in the
-- src:3652 | constitution of a company that may be incorporated as a private
-- src:3653 | company.
@ref s 18(4) (src:3642-3653)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration is made by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration is of a restriction on the right to transfer its shares or of a limitation on the number of its members, included or deemed to be included in its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after the alteration the constitution ceases to include the limitation required by subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(4) the private company may by special resolution make the alteration` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `the alteration is made by special resolution` AND `the alteration is of a restriction on the right to transfer its shares or of a limitation on the number of its members, included or deemed to be included in its constitution`
    THEN (IF `after the alteration the constitution ceases to include the limitation required by subsection (1)(b)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not so that the constitution of the company ceases to include the limitation required by subsection (1)(b)" (a proviso, met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may, by special resolution, alter any restriction ... or any limitation ..."; the text says nothing of any other company, way or alteration

§ `Regulative rules of ss 17 and 18`

DECLARE `s 17 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 17(6) elect to convert and re-register the company either as a company limited by shares or as a company limited by guarantee`
    `s 17(9) issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation`

-- A DEADLINE: "within 2 years of that date" (15 August 1984, which is time 0): 730 days.
-- src:3569 | (6) The prohibition referred to in subsection (5) does not affect a
-- src:3570 | company limited by guarantee which has a share capital and is
-- src:3571 | registered as such before 15 August 1984 and section 38(2) continues
-- src:3572 | to apply to a company so registered; but any such company must,
-- src:3573 | within 2 years of that date, elect to convert and re‑register that
-- src:3574 | company either as a company limited by shares or as a company
-- src:3575 | limited by guarantee.
@ref s 17(6) (src:3569-3575)
GIVEN bearer IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 17 act`
`s 17(6) rule: the company's duty to elect to convert and re-register` MEANS
    PARTY bearer
    MUST `s 17(6) elect to convert and re-register the company either as a company limited by shares or as a company limited by guarantee`
    WITHIN 730
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY bearer BECAUSE "the company did not elect, within 2 years of 15 August 1984, to convert and re-register as a company limited by shares or as a company limited by guarantee"

-- src:3599 | (9) Upon the application of a company and payment of the
-- src:3600 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a
-- src:3601 | certificate of confirmation of incorporation.
@ref s 17(9) (src:3599-3601)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 17 act`
`s 17(9) rule: the Registrar's duty to issue the certificate of confirmation of incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 17(9) issue to the company a certificate of confirmation of incorporation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 17(9) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue the certificate of confirmation of incorporation" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
